%N A400693 Sum of cubes of A069268: a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} gcd(k!, k*(k+1)/2)^3.
%C A400693 A069268(k) = k*(k+1)/2 unless k+1 is an odd prime p, in which case A069268(k) = (p-1)/2. Hence each odd prime p <= n+1 lowers a(n) below the sum of cubes of triangular numbers by ((p-1)/2)^3*(p^3-1).
%F A400693 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} (k*(k+1)/2)^3 - Sum_{p odd prime, p <= n+1} ((p-1)/2)^3*(p^3-1).
%F A400693 a(n) ~ n^7/56.
%e A400693 a(4) = 1^3 + 1^3 + 6^3 + 2^3 = 226.
%t A400693 Accumulate[Table[GCD[k!, k*(k+1)/2]^3, {k, 30}]]
%o A400693 (Python) from math import gcd, factorial; a = lambda n: sum(gcd(factorial(k), k*(k+1)//2)**3 for k in range(1, n+1))
%Y A400693 Cf. A000217, A069268, A398065, A400687.
%K A400693 nonn,easy,new
%O A400693 1,2
